Blue curve: $y=2\sin(2x)+4$. Red dashed line: $y=1$.

$\begin{aligned}4\cos(2x)-3&=1\\4\cos(2x)&=4\\\cos(2x)&=1\end{aligned}$

Let $u=2x$, so $0\le u\le4\pi$.

Cosine equals $1$ at the start and end of each full revolution. Include both endpoints of the domain.

$u=0,\ 2\pi,\ 4\pi$.

$\begin{aligned}x&=\frac u2\\x&=0,\ \pi,\ 2\pi\end{aligned}$

The line $y=1$ meets the curve at its three maxima in the domain.

